# tests/bench/valgrind.supp -- Memcheck suppressions for `make leak`.
#
# The compiler's startup prologue makes two process-lifetime allocations in
# generated main and never frees them, DELIBERATELY: the argv rows
# (bootstrap/gen_c.py:2052) and the root arena state (the first
# `env.mem.alloc()` in src/zen/zen.zen). Both live exactly as long as the
# process and the OS reclaims them. At -O2 both sit inline in `main`, so
# valgrind reports them as definite leaks two frames deep.
#
# The shape of this block is the honesty: only a malloc called DIRECTLY from
# main is suppressed. Any leak one frame deeper -- parser, sema, gen_c --
# still fails `make leak`.
{
   zen_startup_argv_rows_and_root_arena
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:malloc
   fun:main
}
